      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please simplify `stuck_ara_read_cb` and strengthen `test_handle_irqs_limit`:\n\n1. **Remove dead branching and magic numbers in `stuck_ara_read_cb`**: With `handle_irqs()` bounded to 10 iterations, `*read_count \u003c STUCK_IRQ_MAX_ARA_READS` (`50`) is always true and the `return -EIO;` fallback branch is unreachable dead code. Removing `STUCK_IRQ_MAX_ARA_READS` and the `if` branch keeps the test callback minimal and branch-free.\n2. **Share the limit constant**: By defining `RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT` in `zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.h` and including `\"drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.h\"`, you can drop the duplicated `#define STUCK_IRQ_EXPECTED_LIMIT 10`.\n3. **Assert before cleanup and verify early exit when IRQ deasserts (`any_irq_gpio_asserted()`)**: Assert `ara_read_count \u003d\u003d RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT` immediately after `k_msleep(TEST_WAIT_FOR_INTERVAL_MS)` before resetting the read callback and re-pulsing the IRQ. In addition, because `emul_pdc_pulse_irq()` leaves the active-low GPIO asserted (`0`), `any_irq_gpio_asserted()` never evaluates to `false` in existing tests; also testing that `handle_irqs()` stops before the limit when the IRQ GPIO deasserts (e.g., on the `(RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT - 1)`th ARA read) isolates both clauses of `while (any_irq_gpio_asserted() \u0026\u0026 --limit \u003e 0)`.\n\n```c\nstruct stuck_ara_ctx {\n\tint read_count;\n\tint deassert_after_reads;\n};\n\nstatic int stuck_ara_read_cb(const struct emul *target, int reg, uint8_t *val,\n\t\t\t     int bytes, void *data)\n{\n\tstruct stuck_ara_ctx *ctx \u003d data;\n\tconst struct i2c_dt_spec i2c_spec \u003d I2C_DT_SPEC_GET(RTS5453P_NODE);\n\tconst struct gpio_dt_spec irq_gpio \u003d\n\t\tGPIO_DT_SPEC_GET(RTS5453P_NODE, irq_gpios);\n\n\tARG_UNUSED(target);\n\tARG_UNUSED(reg);\n\tARG_UNUSED(bytes);\n\n\tctx-\u003eread_count++;\n\t*val \u003d i2c_spec.addr \u003c\u003c 1;\n\tif (ctx-\u003eread_count \u003d\u003d ctx-\u003edeassert_after_reads) {\n\t\tgpio_emul_input_set(irq_gpio.port, irq_gpio.pin, 1);\n\t}\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\nZTEST_USER(rts54xx, test_handle_irqs_limit)\n{\n\tconst struct emul *ara_emul \u003d EMUL_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(smbus_ara_emul));\n\tstruct i2c_common_emul_data *ara_common \u003d ara_emul-\u003edata;\n\tstruct stuck_ara_ctx ctx \u003d {\n\t\t.read_count \u003d 0,\n\t\t.deassert_after_reads \u003d RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT + 1,\n\t};\n\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_func(ara_common, stuck_ara_read_cb, \u0026ctx);\n\n\t/* Pulse IRQ (leaves active-low GPIO asserted) while ARA keeps\n\t * responding. Verify handle_irqs() bounds the loop to\n\t * RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT iterations.\n\t */\n\tzassert_ok(emul_pdc_pulse_irq(emul));\n\tk_msleep(TEST_WAIT_FOR_INTERVAL_MS);\n\tzassert_equal(ctx.read_count, RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT,\n\t\t      \"handle_irqs looped %d times without yielding\",\n\t\t      ctx.read_count);\n\n\t/* Verify handle_irqs() stops early as soon as the IRQ GPIO deasserts\n\t * before reaching RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT.\n\t */\n\tctx.read_count \u003d 0;\n\tctx.deassert_after_reads \u003d RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT - 1;\n\tzassert_ok(emul_pdc_pulse_irq(emul));\n\tk_msleep(TEST_WAIT_FOR_INTERVAL_MS);\n\tzassert_equal(ctx.read_count, RTS54XX_MAX_IRQ_LOOP_COUNT - 1);\n\n\t/* Restore normal ARA read handler and drain the queued ARA entry. */\n\ti2c_common_emul_set_read_func(ara_common, NULL, NULL);\n\tzassert_ok(emul_pdc_pulse_irq(emul));\n\tzassert_ok(emul_pdc_idle_wait(emul));\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/d23afc59-c1db-4742-8f70-262543e846f7)",
